From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:46:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: give the app the id of what we sent to a group
 elsewhere

A message we sent to a group from another client, the Telegram app on
the phone say, reached the Messaging app without its serviceMessageId:
a poll made on the phone could not be voted in from the app, nor such
a message reacted to or edited. showMessageTextChat stashed
"webos-msg-id" on the conversation for a received group message only;
a private chat's such message has had it all along.

It is written with purple_conv_chat_write under our own name, which
libpurple (2.14, conversation.c, purple_conv_chat_write) compares with
the chat's nick. That is the account's user name, the phone number,
where the name we write under is the account's alias, our full name,
so libpurple adds PURPLE_MESSAGE_RECV and the transport stores the
message as a received one. Either way the transport's
incoming_message_cb takes the stash with the write: as a received
message's, or as an outgoing carbon's (PURPLE_MESSAGE_REMOTE_SEND).

What this client sent itself is still not stashed: the app has it, and
its id comes with "webos-im-outbox-id" once TDLib has sent it.

Unit test in test/webos-commands-test.cpp.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
---
 receiving.cpp                |  9 ++++++++-
 test/webos-commands-test.cpp | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 43 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/receiving.cpp b/receiving.cpp
index 0ef67cc..bd7fa48 100644
--- a/receiving.cpp
+++ b/receiving.cpp
@@ -651,9 +651,16 @@ static void showMessageTextChat(TdAccountData &account, const td::td_api::chat &
 
     if (text) {
         if (flags & PURPLE_MESSAGE_SEND) {
-            if (conv)
+            if (conv) {
+                // webOS: as for a private chat's, stash the id of what we sent from another client
+                // (the transport's incoming_message_cb takes it with the write), so that the
+                // message can be reacted to, voted in or edited from the app.
+                if (serviceMessageId && *serviceMessageId)
+                    purple_conversation_set_data(purple_conv_chat_get_conversation(conv), "webos-msg-id",
+                                                 g_strdup(serviceMessageId));
                 purple_conv_chat_write(conv, purple_account_get_name_for_display(account.purpleAccount),
                                        text, flags, message.timestamp);
+            }
         } else {
             if (purpleId != 0) {
                 // webOS: smuggle the sender's routable id + display name through the single `who` slot
diff --git a/test/webos-commands-test.cpp b/test/webos-commands-test.cpp
index 5e4072b..6bd61dd 100644
--- a/test/webos-commands-test.cpp
+++ b/test/webos-commands-test.cpp
@@ -1236,6 +1236,41 @@ TEST_F(WebosCommandTest, VotePollNotSent)
     );
 }
 
+// What we sent to a group from another client is shown with its id, as a received message is, so
+// that the app can react to it, edit it or vote in it. libpurple writes it as received, our name
+// being no member's of the chat, and the transport stores it so.
+TEST_F(WebosCommandTest, OwnMessageFromElsewhereInGroup)
+{
+    login();
+    addBasicGroup();
+    tgl.update(make_object<updateNewMessage>(makeMessage(
+        1, userIds[0], groupChatId, false, 10001, makeTextMessage("Lunch?")
+    )));
+    tgl.verifyRequest(viewMessages(groupChatId, {1}, nullptr, true));
+    prpl.discardEvents();
+    PurpleConversation *conv = purple_find_chat(connection, 2);
+    ASSERT_NE(nullptr, conv);
+    char *stashed = static_cast<char *>(purple_conversation_get_data(conv, "webos-msg-id"));
+    ASSERT_STREQ(serviceMessageId(groupChatId, 1).c_str(), stashed);
+    // The transport takes it, with the write
+    g_free(stashed);
+    purple_conversation_set_data(conv, "webos-msg-id", nullptr);
+
+    // Sent elsewhere: TDLib has no sending state for it
+    auto message = makeMessage(2, selfId, groupChatId, true, 10002, makeTextMessage("At one"));
+    message->sending_state_ = nullptr;
+    tgl.update(make_object<updateNewMessage>(std::move(message)));
+    tgl.verifyRequest(viewMessages(groupChatId, {2}, nullptr, true));
+    prpl.verifyEvents(ConversationWriteEvent(
+        groupChatPurpleName, selfFirstName + " " + selfLastName, "At one",
+        (PurpleMessageFlags)(PURPLE_MESSAGE_SEND | PURPLE_MESSAGE_REMOTE_SEND), 10002
+    ));
+    stashed = static_cast<char *>(purple_conversation_get_data(conv, "webos-msg-id"));
+    ASSERT_STREQ(serviceMessageId(groupChatId, 2).c_str(), stashed);
+    g_free(stashed);
+    purple_conversation_set_data(conv, "webos-msg-id", nullptr);
+}
+
 // A group's own news is told in words, not as "Unsupported message type"
 TEST_F(WebosCommandTest, GroupEvents)
 {
